msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Today, we released Quarkus 3.39.3, a maintenance release for our 3.39 "
"release train."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This release contains bugfixes and documentation improvements.\n"
"It should be a safe upgrade for anyone already using 3.39."
msgstr ""

msgid "A notable change in this release is:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/56487[#56487] - Update to Avro 1."
"12.2, auto-trust Avro-generated classes, add properties to configure "
"additional Avro-trusted classes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To update to Quarkus 3.39, we recommend updating to the latest version of "
"the Quarkus CLI and run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that `quarkus update` can update your applications from any version of "
"Quarkus (including 2.x) to Quarkus 3.39."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information about the adjustments you need to make to your "
"applications, please refer to the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/"
"Migration-Guide-3.39[Quarkus 3.39 migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get the full changelog of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/3.39.3[3.39.3] on GitHub."
msgstr ""

msgid "Come Join Us"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We value your feedback a lot so please report bugs, ask for improvements... "
"Let's build something great together!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are a Quarkus user or just curious, don't be shy and join our "
"welcoming community:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"provide feedback on https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues[GitHub];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"craft some code and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pulls[push a PR];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"discuss with us on https://quarkusio.zulipchat.com/[Zulip] and on the https:/"
"/groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-dev[mailing list];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"ask your questions on https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/"
"quarkus[Stack Overflow]."
msgstr ""
